commit 9559e0f91ba8b7af654fdb1249273f72a975a0a8

C03: browser.control opens a new tab in the product's browser (BROWSER1493)

«abrí una pestaña nueva» (H0084) had no operation: browser.control admitted only back, close, fullscreen_video, reload and scrolling. Kernel: the action enum gains `new_tab` (LowReversible, no confirmation). Provider: `ControlAsync("new_tab")` creates a blank page target through the CDP `json/new` endpoint of the product's own browser and verifies it by its presence in `json/list` (`target_created`; `cdp_new_tab_rejected` / `cdp_new_tab_not_verified` otherwise). Mind: `browser_new_tab_arguments` reads «abrí/abre/abrime una (nueva/otra) pestaña (nueva)» and «open a new tab», never with a named browser, a URL, a prohibition or a close; the argument builder grounds `{"action": "new_tab"}`; the composer projects the control result without its target id and instructs the final to say, in the past, that a new empty tab was opened.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


